{"slug":"mark-desaulnier","qid":"Q6767311","name":"Mark DeSaulnier","desc":"American politician","article":"Mark DeSaulnier","born":"1952-03-31","died":null,"birthplace":"Lowell","parties":["Democratic Party","California Democratic Party","Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"CA-10","f":2023,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"CA-11","f":2015,"u":2023},{"t":"California State Senate","w":"","f":2008,"u":2015},{"t":"California State Assembly","w":"","f":2006,"u":2008}],"summary":"Mark James DeSaulnier ( də-SOH-nee-ay; born March 31, 1952) is an American politician who has served as a U.S. representative from California since 2015. He has represented California's 10th congressional district since 2023, although it was previously numbered the 11th district for his first eight years in office. The district includes most of Contra Costa County, a suburban county in the East Bay.","photo":{"f":"mark-desaulnier.jpg","by":"US Congress","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mark_DeSaulnier-1.jpeg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"CA-10","p":"D","n":"Mark DeSaulnier","race":"CA-10"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"CA-10","p":"D","v":242325,"s":66.47,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"CA-10","p":"D","v":198415,"s":78.93,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"CA-11","p":"D","v":271063,"s":72.99,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"CA-11","p":"D","v":204369,"s":74.13,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"CA-11","p":"D","v":214868,"s":72.05,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"CA-11","p":"D","v":117502,"s":67.27,"w":true,"n":"Mark DeSaulnier"}]}